{
  "reason": "The current GRURec achieves macro validation HR@10=0.5737, with Electronics at 0.435, but its independent positive/negative softplus terms do not directly optimize competition among candidates. Historical sampled-softmax experiments support testing a relative-ranking objective, without establishing that it will improve this GRU. Modify loss design and its training-loop implementation only, preserving the successful recurrent architecture and existing sampling to isolate the objective change.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Replace the independent binary logistic objective with sampled-softmax cross-entropy over each valid position's positive and eight existing uniform negatives, placing the positive at class zero. Following the historical sampled-softmax experiment, make candidates compete directly while retaining the current eight-negative configuration to isolate the loss hypothesis. Preserve GRURec, its constructor, encode, score, and predict signatures, and its 96-dimensional embeddings, two GRU layers, tied normalized embeddings, jointly learned item bias and score scale, dropout, and maximum history length; introduce no additional predictors or scoring components.",
    "training_evaluation": "In train_category, retain positive_logits and negative_logits and replace the two softplus reductions with logits = torch.cat([positive_logits.unsqueeze(1), negative_logits], dim=1), followed by nn.functional.cross_entropy(logits.float(), torch.zeros(logits.shape[0], dtype=torch.long, device=device)); each row must represent one position selected by the existing mask. Keep NEGATIVES=8, uniform sampling, target-collision resampling, duplicate-negative behavior, history windowing, optimizer, learning rate, batch size, mixed precision, clipping, epoch limit, deadlines, and early stopping unchanged. Preserve preprocessing seed=0, training seed=42, the supplied splits, all four categories, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and single-GPU execution, with no hidden-test access or external data. Retain fixed validation candidates, 200 users per category, 99 unique negatives, evaluation seed=42, and existing HR@10 checkpoint selection with NDCG tie-breaking; use the pinned host macro HR@10 to assess the hypothesized 0.01–0.02 absolute improvement over 0.5737 and inspect category regressions without assuming success. Preserve train_category and write_predict_script signatures, checkpoint metadata, trial-local artifacts, dataset routing, and identical validation/prediction preprocessing; the unchanged predictor writer must continue loading exactly one newly trained checkpoint per category without averaging or checkpoint reuse."
  }
}
